---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContentSection from "../components/ContentSection.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Pilgrimage Homeschool">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <h1>About Us</h1>
    <p class="hero-lede">
      Learn more about the Pilgrimage Homeschool Science Olympiad team.
    </p>
  </section>

  <ContentSection title="What is Science Olympiad?">
    <p>
      Science Olympiad is a competition for elementary, middle, and high school
      students that focuses on many different aspects of science and technology.
      Teams of up to 15 students compete in pairs of two or three, to complete
      tests, build gadgets, and try to get the top score in their event. There
      are 23 different events and a total team score is calculated from the team
      scores in the 23 events.
    </p>
    <p>
      The top 14 teams at a regional tournament move on to the state finals, and
      from there, one team will emerge state champion. The state champion moves
      on to compete at the national tournament. What makes Science Olympiad so
      fun is that you can do anything from building a working glider plane, to
      cracking toxicology cases in “Crime Busters," to looking at natural
      history in “Fossils!”
    </p>
  </ContentSection>

  <ContentSection title="Our History">
    <p>
      The Pilgrimage Homeschool Science Olympiad team was established in 2010 as
      a middle school (Division B) team and has been one of the
      highest-performing teams in the state, competing continuously for the last
      16 seasons.
    </p>
    <p>
      Though our team has never had formal funding or corporate sponsors, we
      have won #1 in the state four of twelve times (Division B in 2014, 15, &
      17, and Division C in 2015), competing for Maryland at nationals. Since
      then, Pilgrimage Div B has won every season in the top 5 at the state
      tournament.
    </p>
    <p>
      Maryland's high school team was established in 2013 and has competed in
      eight seasons since. In 2023, Pilgrimage Homeschool expanded to include an
      elementary school (Division A) team. As of the 2023 season, homeschoolers
      in grades 3 - 12 are eligible to compete with the team.
    </p>
  </ContentSection>
</BaseLayout>
